# THIS FILE DOES NOT GOVERN THE API IMAGE BUILD. Read this before editing it.
#
# docker/Dockerfile.apiserver is built with the PARENT directory as its context -- the one holding
# both graphql-api/ and ncog-evm/ -- because go.mod carries
#     replace github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum => ../ncog-evm
# and Docker reads the ignore file for the CONTEXT, not for the repo. The filter that actually
# trims that build is docker/Dockerfile.apiserver.dockerignore, a per-Dockerfile ignore file that
# BuildKit resolves in preference to the context-root one. Edit that file.
#
# This one applies only to a `docker build` whose context is this repository, of which there is
# none: such a build cannot resolve ../ncog-evm and fails with
#     failed to compute cache key: "/ncog-evm": not found
# It is kept so that mistake costs a fast failure instead of uploading 50 MB of Windows binaries,
# the git history and a live config file to the daemon first -- and so any future single-repo
# build starts from a sane baseline rather than shipping all of that into a layer.
#
# Patterns are anchored at this repo's root and are not recursive.

.git
.github
.idea
.vscode

# Build artefacts. apiserver.exe and migrate.exe are 35 MB and 15 MB, gitignored via *.exe and so
# invisible to git-based hygiene, and sitting right beside go.mod.
*.exe
*.test
build
vendor

# Local configuration. internal/config/load.go searches "." for a file named "apiserver", so a
# config in this directory is loaded automatically -- and doc/postgres-cutover.md documents exactly
# that file carrying a live PostgreSQL DSN.
apiserver.json
apiserver.yaml
apiserver.yml
apiserver.toml
.env
.env.*

*.log
*.prof
.DS_Store
